  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Estriol and Dipeptidyl peptidase IX (DPPX) through a series of target interactions. Estriol is implicated in the pathway as a target of multiple compounds, including Rupicolin B, Ribisin D, and Hydroxysaikosaponin C, all of which are themselves targets of DPPX. This indicates that Estriol may interact with DPPX via these intermediaries, potentially through a common mechanism involving the regulation of ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2. The high scores across the three paths (final_score=0.7347) suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible regulatory or inhibitory role of Estriol in modulating DPPX activity, though further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction.",
